Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 08:15:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 042/105] qwen4-exp mtp: placeholder draft vocab weights
 (SGLANG_DRAFT_SKIP_VOCAB_WEIGHTS)

The NEXTN draft allocated a full [248320, 2560] BF16 embed_tokens and an
identical lm_head at construction -- 2.37 GB that no checkpoint tensor ever
fills (the Qwen4-Exp checkpoint carries no mtp.embed_tokens /
mtp.shared_head.head rows) and that eagle_worker_v2.init_lm_head then throws
away, replacing both with the target's tensors. On a 96 GB card with the
target resident that pair is the start-up peak: the 1.19 GiB embed allocation
is what OOMs when the desktop takes ~0.8 GB more than usual.

Behind SGLANG_DRAFT_SKIP_VOCAB_WEIGHTS the two modules are built on the meta
device -- keeping their real layout metadata and quant method -- and get a
1-row placeholder weight for set_embed_and_head to del and replace. Measured
w4/w16: draft-phase mem usage -10.76 GB vs -8.36 GB, i.e. 2.40 GB less
resident, with needle, sanity_gen and greedy acceptance (prose-en 2.58,
agent-loop 3.19 vs 2.54 / 3.24) unchanged.

Default off: the freed bytes sit inside the mem_fraction_static budget, so the
KV pool grows to claim them (w4 722688 -> 839360 tokens) and a deployment
tuned against the old footprint loses that much runtime headroom -- w16 at
--mem-fraction-static 0.97 starts but OOMs on the first request until the
fraction comes down to ~0.945.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
